    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** leading the charge as our premier option at a 70.48 efficiency score. Facing Sproat, **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a favorable matchup against an average starter and a prime #4 spot in the order, offering the highest floor and ceiling combination in our outfield. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** follows closely at 65.00; while his platoon edge against Keller is neutral-to-negative, his elite xwOBA of 0.378 and central spot in the lineup make him a primary engine for our RBI and HR production. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a tactical must-start at 63.79; despite a negative platoon shift against Valdez, his ability to capitalize on the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery significantly increases his stolen base equity\u2014our most critical scarcity category\u2014solidifying his role despite the unfavorable handedness.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Josh Jung** on the bench. With a score of 42.59, **Josh Jung** fell just short of the 45-point threshold required to displace the lower-end starters. While he would typically benefit from a #3 lineup slot, the optimizer penalized him heavily for the 3.23 xERA of Detmers, viewing the matchup as too restrictive compared to the upside offered by **Jackson Merrill** (61.54) and **Miguel Vargas** (58.06). We are also monitoring **Coby Mayo**, whose 51.56 score is anchored by a high park factor; however, his inclusion is contingent on his official confirmation in the #8 spot. Should he be scratched or shifted further down the order, his utility value will evaporate quickly, necessitating a pivot to our remaining bench depth.\n\nWe have officially ruled out **Jordan Westburg** and **Jorge Polanco** due to their ongoing IL designations, forcing us to lean heavily on the speed-oriented profiles of **Nasim Nunez** and **Brayan Rocchio**. While **Nasim Nunez** (55.68) provides essential stolen base potential against the left-handed Perez, we acknowledge the risk inherent in his #8 spot. Similarly, **Liam Hicks** (51.54) is being started primarily for his leadoff placement, though he faces a rigorous test against Scott. We will continue to evaluate the late-day weather reports to ensure that our exposure remains optimized for maximum efficiency across all five categories, particularly as we monitor **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Josh Lowe**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Dominic Smith**, **Gage Workman**, and **Drake Baldwin** for any late-breaking roster pivots.",
